WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.519
Part (c), three marks.

00:00:01.519 --> 00:00:07.939
Yellow highlight: two uppercase letters plus four digits, for example A B one two three four.

00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:12.427
This validation is a format check; a type check is also accepted.

00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:17.191
Purpose: make codes match the set pattern and keep invalid codes out.

00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:20.090
Or: improve data accuracy and consistency.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:26.856
Do not answer verification or range check — this is about a character pattern, not numeric bounds.
